 ],
 "about": "IAM-Atlas v2.1 was fitted the way a sky map is: every site carries 100 equally likely versions of each cell's healthy map (posterior draws, Zenodo 10.5281/zenodo.23422688). Any one draw is speckled with noise; averaging more draws beats it down, about as one over the square root of their number, which is how the microwave sky's noise is beaten down by more observing. Slide from 1 draw to 100 and watch the speckle fade; what stays bright longest is where the atlas is least sure. Draws are taken in turn from the fit's four sampling chains.",
